.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt SFCAPD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sfcapd
.Nd sFlow collector for sFlow v2/v4 and v5
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm 
.Fl w Ar flowdir
.Op Fl C Ar config
.Op Fl z=<compress>
.Op Fl D
.Op Fl u Ar userid
.Op Fl g Ar groupid
.Op Fl S Ar num
.Op Fl t Ar interval
.Op Fl P Ar pidfile
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl d Ar device
.Op Fl I Ar ident
.Op Fl b Ar bindhost
.Op Fl f Ar flowfile
.Op Fl 4
.Op Fl 6
.Op Fl J Ar mcastgroup
.Op Fl R Ar repeater
.Op Fl H Ar host[/port]
.Op Fl A
.Op Fl B Ar buffsize|auto
.Op Fl n Ar sourceparam
.Op Fl M Ar multiflowdir
.Op Fl i Ar metricrate
.Op Fl m Ar metricpath
.Op Fl o Ar optionlist
.Op Fl e
.Op Fl l Ar command
.Op Fl x Ar key=value
.Op Fl X Ar extensionList
.Op Fl F Ar filter
.Op Fl W Ar num
.Op Fl K Ns Oo = Ns Ar passphrase | Pf @ Ar keyfile Oc
.Op Fl k Ns Oo = Ns Ar passphrase | Pf @ Ar keyfile Oc
.Op Fl N Ar seconds
.Op Fl Q Ar bits
.Op Fl v Ar level
.Op Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads sFlow data from the network and stores the records into binary formatted
files. Packet samples are converted into nfdump-compatible flow records.
.Pp
The 1.8.x collector uses the rewritten sFlow decoder and the shared threaded
V3 backend. Its receive, rotation, forwarding, and encrypted-backend behavior
matches the corresponding nfcapd facilities where the protocols apply.
.Pp
If you want to collect NetFlow data, please have a look at
.Ar nfcapd
which is also part of the nfdump tools. 
.Pp
sFlow is an industry standard developed by InMon Corporation. For more information see http://sflow.org.
.Pp
.Nm 
shares the common collector features of
.Xr nfcapd 1 .
See also
.Xr nfcapd 1
for details.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl w Ar flowdir
Set the flow directory to store the output files. If a sub hierarchy is specified with
.Fl S
the final directory is concatenated to flowdir/subdir.
.It Fl C Ar config
Reads additional configuration parameters from
.Ar config
file.
.Nm
tries to read the config file from the install default path 
.Ar $prefix/etc/
which may be overwritten by the environment variable
.Ar NFCONF
, which again is overwritten by this option
.Fl C.
If
.Fl C Ar none
is specified, then no config file is read, even if found in the search path.
.It Fl p Ar portnum
Set the port number to listen. Default port is 9995
.It Fl d Ar interface
Reads sFlow packets from a capture interface. Requires a build configured
with \fB--enable-readpcap\fR.
.It Fl f Ar pcapfile
Reads sFlow datagrams from an offline pcap file. Requires a build configured
with \fB--enable-readpcap\fR.
.It Fl b Ar bindhost
Specifies the hostname/IPv4/IPv6 address to bind for listening. This can be an IP address or a hostname, 
resolving to a local IP address.
.It Fl 4
Forces
.Nm
to listen on IPv4 addresses only. Can be used together with -b if a hostname has IPv4 and IPv6 addresses.
.It Fl 6
Forces
.Nm
to listen on IPv6 addresses only. Can be used together with -b if a hostname has IPv4 and IPv6 addresses.
.It Fl J Ar mcastgroup
Join the specified IPv4 or IPv6 multicast group for listening.
.It Fl R Ar host[/port]
Enables the packet repeater. All incoming packets are sent additionally to another
.Ar host
and
.Ar port .
.Ar host
is either a valid IPv4/IPv6 address, or a symbolic hostname, which resolves to a valid IP address.
.Ar port
may be omitted and defaults to 9995. Note: As IPv4/IPv6 are accepted the host/port separator is '/'.
Only one repeater may be defined. Use this method to daisy chain collectors.
.It Fl H Ar host[/port]
Forward all collected flows to a remote
.Xr nfcapd 1
collector via UDP instead of writing them to local files.
.Ar host
is a valid IPv4/IPv6 address or hostname.
.Ar port
may be omitted and defaults to 9995.
The separator between host and port is '/' to avoid ambiguity with IPv6 addresses.
Flows are sent using nfdump wire format protocol v250 (plain) or v251 (encrypted, see
.Fl k
below).
The file-compression options
.Fl z
apply only to local nffile output and are ignored with
.Fl H .
This option is mutually exclusive with
.Fl w ,
.Fl n ,
and
.Fl M .
Dynamic flow sources
.Pq Fl M
are not supported when
.Fl H
is active.
The UDP send threshold (the inner-payload size that triggers a packet flush)
can be raised past its 1200-byte default via
.Sy udp.sendThreshold
in
.Xr nfdump.conf 5 ,
useful on paths with a larger MTU (jumbo frames, tunnels, loopback) to send
fewer, larger packets for the same flow volume.
.It Fl A
Sets source address spoofing mode for the repeater. The source address of the repeated packets
is set to the original IP address. This needs
.Nm
to be started with root privileges. Please note, that source spoofing may be blocked by firewalls or
routers in your network.
.It Fl I Ar ident
Sets
.Ar ident
as identification string for the current source. This string is written into the output file to identify
the source. Default is 'none'. If you have multiple sources, see option
.Fl n
below.
.It Fl n Ar 'ident,IPList,flowdir'
Configures an sFlow source identified by the string
.Ar ident,IPList,flowdir .
The
.Ar IPList
is a semicolon-separated list of one or more IP addresses or CIDR blocks, and may include both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses. For example:
.Dl -n 'router1,192.0.2.1;2001:db8::1/64,in'
.Pp
Note that the entire argument must be enclosed in single quotes to prevent the shell from interpreting the semicolon as a command separator.
.Pp
This option also acts as a filter: only packets originating from IP addresses listed in
.Ar IPList
will be accepted. Packets from sources not matching any entry in the list are silently discarded.
.Pp
If you have multiple sources per collector, specify multiple
.Fl n
options. All exporters send their flows to the same port specified with
.Fl p .
Do not mix single-source configuration using
.Fl I
with multiple
.Fl n
options.
.It Fl M Ar flowdir
Set the flow directory for dynamically allocated exporters. New exporters are dynamically added when sending data.
All exporters send sFlow data to the same port and IP. For each dynamically added source, a new subdirectory
is created under 
.Ar flowdir
with the name of the IP address of the exporter. All '.' and ':" in IP addresses are replaced by '-'.
.It Fl D
Set daemon mode: fork to background and detach from terminal.
.Nm
terminates on signal TERM, INT or HUP.
.It Fl P Ar pidfile
Writes the running process ID into
.Ar pidfile .
Use this option to integrate
.Nm
in start/stop files.
.It Fl u Ar userid
Drop privileges of running process to user
.Ar userid .
.Nm
needs to be started as user root.
.It Fl g Ar groupid
Drop privileges of running process to group
.Ar groupid .
.Nm
needs to be started as user root.
.It Fl B Ar bufflen|auto
Sets the network socket input buffer to
.Ar bufflen
bytes. For high-volume traffic it is recommended to raise this value to typically more than 100 kB,
otherwise you risk to lose packets. The default is OS (and kernel) dependent.
The special value
.Cm auto
probes progressively larger values, up to a 100 MiB request limit, and keeps the largest effective
.Dv SO_RCVBUF
the kernel grants. The effective value is logged at startup.
.It Fl S Ar num
Adds an additional directory subhierarchy to store the data files. The default is 0, no
subhierarchy, which means all files go directly into
.Ar flowdir .
The 
.Ar flowdir
is concatenated with the specified sub hierarchy format to create the final data directory.
The following hierarchies are defined:
.Bl -item -compact
.It
0 default     no hierarchy levels
.It
1 %Y/%m/%d    year/month/day
.It
2 %Y/%m/%d/%H year/month/day/hour
.It
3 %Y/%W/%u    year/week_of_year/day_of_week
.It
4 %Y/%W/%u/%H year/week_of_year/day_of_week/hour
.It
5 %Y/%j       year/day-of-year
.It
6 %Y/%j/%H    year/day-of-year/hour
.It
7 %Y-%m-%d    year-month-day
.It
8 %Y-%m-%d/%H year-month-day/hour
.El
.It Fl t Ar interval
Sets the time interval in seconds to rotate files. The default value is 300 seconds (five minutes).
The smallest available interval is 2s.
.It Fl z=lzo
Compress flow files with LZO1X-1 compression. Fastest compression.
.It Fl z=bz2
Compress flow files with bz2 compression. Slow but most efficient. It is not recommended 
to use bz2 for real-time capture.
.It Fl z=lz4[:level]
Compress flow files with LZ4 compression. Fast and efficient. Optional level should be between 1..10
Changing the level results in smaller files but uses up more time to compress. Levels > 5 may need more
CPU cores. See -W.
.It Fl z=zstd[:level]
Compress flow files with ZSTD compression. Fast and efficient. Optional level should be between 1..10
Changing the level results in smaller files but uses up more time to compress. Levels > 5 may need more
CPU cores. See -W.
.It Fl K Ns Oo = Ns Ar passphrase | Pf @ Ar keyfile Oc
Encrypt all output flow files using ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD authenticated encryption.
Requires
.Nm
to be compiled with libsodium support.
.Pp
The passphrase may be supplied in one of three ways:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl K Ns = Ns Ar passphrase
Use
.Ar passphrase
directly.
The
.Ql =
is required; there must be no space between
.Fl K
and the passphrase.
.It Fl K Ns Pf @ Ar keyfile
Read the passphrase from the first line of
.Ar keyfile .
Trailing newlines are stripped.
This avoids exposing the passphrase in the process table.
.It Fl K
(no argument) Prompt interactively from the terminal with echo disabled.
.El
.Pp
The encryption key is derived from the passphrase using Argon2id
.Pq Li crypto_pwhash
with a freshly generated random per-file salt, so every rotated output file uses a distinct
derived key.
Encrypted files can be read and decrypted with
.Xr nfdump 1
using the same
.Fl K
option.
.It Fl k Ns Oo = Ns Ar passphrase | Pf @ Ar keyfile Oc
Enable authenticated encryption for UDP flow transport when forwarding to a remote collector
.Pq Fl H
using XChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD authenticated encryption (nfd wire format v251).
Requires
.Nm
to be compiled with libsodium support.
.Fl k
derives a 32-byte session key from the passphrase via Argon2id and sends flows
as protocol version 251.
The receiving
.Xr nfcapd 1
must be started with the same passphrase via
.Fl k .
.Pp
The passphrase may be supplied in one of three ways:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ns = Ns Ar passphrase
Use
.Ar passphrase
directly.
The
.Ql =
is required; there must be no space between
.Fl k
and the passphrase.
.It Fl k Ns Pf @ Ar keyfile
Read the passphrase from the first line of
.Ar keyfile .
Trailing newlines are stripped.
.It Fl k
(no argument) Prompt interactively from the terminal with echo disabled.
.El
.It Fl N Ar seconds
Set the epoch-based UDP transport rekey interval for encrypted forwarding.
Requires
.Fl H
and
.Fl k .
The value must be in the range 0 through 604800 seconds; 0 disables rekeying.
It overrides
.Sy crypt.rekeyIntervalSecs
from the
.Sy [common]
section of
.Xr nfdump.conf 5 .
.It Fl Q Ar bits
Set the UDP anti-replay window width to a power of two from 64 through 1024
bits. Requires
.Fl H
and
.Fl k .
It overrides
.Sy crypt.antiReplayWindowBits
from the
.Sy [common]
section of
.Xr nfdump.conf 5 .
The receiving collector applies the anti-replay window; its setting may be
configured independently.
.Pp
Before deriving the forwarding key, sfcapd also applies
.Sy crypt.salt
from the
.Sy [common]
section when present. The forwarding sender and receiving collector must use
the same passphrase and salt.
.It Fl W Ar num
Set the core limit to
.Ar num
CPU cores.
The number of writer threads used to compress and write flow files is derived
automatically from this budget and the chosen codec.
Setting
.Ar num
to 0 (the default) uses all available online CPU cores.
If
.Ar num
exceeds the number of online CPU cores, a warning is logged and the budget
is clamped to the available core count.
.Pp
The writer count can be overridden per-run with
.Fl x Ar threads.writers=N
(0 restores the auto-derived count) or via the
.Em [threads]
section in
.Xr nfdump.conf 5 .
.It Fl e
Sets auto-expire mode. At the end of every rotate interval
.Fl t
.Nm
runs an expire cycle to delete files according to the persisted lifetime and
size limits configured with
.Xr nfexpire 1 .
This option requires local file output
.Pq Fl w , Fl n , or Fl M
and cannot be combined with flow forwarding
.Pq Fl H
or the timezone filename suffix
.Pq Fl Z .
Offline file readers disable auto-expire.
.It Fl x Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value
Override a configuration key for this invocation only. May be repeated.
Overrides have higher priority than the configuration file and program defaults.
For example,
.Dl sfcapd -x threads.writers=4 -w /var/nfdump/flows
.It Fl l Ar command
At the end of every
.Fl t
interval and after the file rotate has completed, 
.Nm
runs the command
.Ar command .
The string for
.Ar command
may contain the following place holders, which are expanded before running:
.Bl -item -compact
.It
%f   File name of new data file including any sub hierarchy.
.It
%d   Top 
.Ar flowdir .
The full path of the new file is: %d/%f
.It
%t   Time slot string in ISO format e.g. 201107110845.
.It
%u   Time slot string in UNIX time format.
.It
%i   Identification string
.Ar ident
string supplied by
.Fl I
.El
.It Fl X Ar extensionList
.Ar extensionList
is a ',' separated list of extensions to be stored by
.Nm .
The numbers correspond to the extension list in nfxV3.h. By default extensions are added 
dynamically to store all data sent by the exporter. If
.Ar extensionList 
is given, only those elements matching the extension are processed and stored. Usually this
option is not needed, unless for specific requirements.
.It Fl F Ar filter
Apply a post-decode record filter before flows are stored
.Pq Fl w , Fl n , Fl M
or forwarded
.Pq Fl H .
Non-matching records are discarded and never reach the backend.
.Ar filter
uses the same filter syntax as
.Xr nfdump 1 ,
restricted to plain element filters on fields already present in the flow record:
IP address/network/list, port, protocol, byte/packet counters, TCP flags, VLAN,
MPLS, AS number, engine/exporter fields, time ranges, and similar direct
comparisons or boolean combinations thereof. Filter primitives that need a
resource outside the record itself
.Po
geo country lookup, Tor exit-node lookup, and timezone lookup, all backed by the
MaxMind/Tor databases, plus payload content matching:
.Cm payload dns ,
.Cm payload ssl , ja3 , ja4 ,
and
.Cm payload regex
.Pc
are rejected with an error at filter-compile time; startup then fails immediately
rather than silently collecting unfiltered or ignoring the filter.
The query-context primitives
.Cm ident
and
.Cm count
are also rejected: they are not fields of an individual V4 record.
The filter is compiled once at startup and evaluated by a single thread per flow
source, so a
.Fl F
filter has no measurable effect on collectors run without it.
.It Fl o Ar options
Set
.Nm
options. This is a ',' separated list of options. Available options:
.Pp
.Sy tun
Enable TUN tunnel decoding.
.Pp
These options may also be defined in the
.Sy nfdump.conf
config file. Options specified on the command line overwrite the value in the config file.
.It Fl m Ar metricpath
Enables the flow metric exporter. Flow metric information is sent to the UNIX socket
.Ar metricpath
at the rate specified by
.Fl i
This option may be used to export flow metric information to other systems such as InfluxDB or Prometheus.
Please note: The flow metric does not include the full record. Only the flow statistics is sent.
.It Fl i Ar metricrate
Sets the interval for the flow metric exporter. This interval may be different from the file rotation
interval
.Ar t 
and is therefore independent from file rotation.
.It Fl v Ar level
Set verbose level. Accepted 0 to 4. The default level is 1 with moderate information. Use -v 3 to
print sFlow records in raw format while collecting. Please note that not all elements
are printed. This option is for debugging purposes only, to verify that incoming sFlow data is processed correctly.
.It Fl Z
Append the local timezone offset to rotated file names.
.It Fl V
Print
.Nm 
version and exit.
.It Fl h
Print help text on stdout with all options and exit.
.El
.Sh SECURITY
.Nm
parses network data supplied by exporters and should be exposed only to trusted
sources. Bind it to the intended collector address and enforce a source-address
allowlist in the host or network firewall. The
.Fl n
source filter provides an additional application-level restriction, but does not
replace firewall filtering.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
returns 0 on success and 255 if initialization failed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
http://sflow.org
.Pp
https://sflow.org/developers/licensing.php
.Pp
https://github.com/sflow/sflowtool
.Pp
.Xr nfdump 1
.Xr nfcapd 1
.Xr nfpcapd 1
.Sh BUGS
